{{also|granulé}}
==English==
{{wikipedia|Granule}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|LL.}} {{term|granulum}}, diminutive of {{etyl|la}} {{term|granum||grain|lang=la}}; see [[grain]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈɡɹanjuːl/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈɡɻænjəl/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A tiny [[grain]], a small [[particle]].
# {{biology}} A small [[structure]] in a [[cell]].
# {{geology}} A [[particle]] from 2 to 4 [[mm]] in [[diameter]], following the [[Wentworth scale]]
# {{astronomy}} a small [[mark]] in the [[photosphere]] of the [[sun]] caused by [[convection]] [[current]]s. See also [[Wikipedia:Granule (solar physics)]].

====Related terms====
* [[grain]]
* [[granular]]
* [[granularity]]
* [[granulate]]
* [[granulation]]

